      "message": "Both conversions look right to me, and the file still needs `\u003clinux/p3s_user_pages.h\u003e` for the MGLRU walk.\n\nCould the body say what fails without this? As far as I can see, it goes back to aosp/4312494, which opted `mm/vmscan.c` into `\u003clinux/p3s_user_pages.h\u003e`, so `PAGE_SIZE` and `PAGE_SHIFT` here follow the current task. A 4KB task that writes `1M` to `memory.reclaim` then asks for 256 kernel pages, i.e. 4MB, and with MGLRU disabled (GKI enables it by default), its direct reclaim computes `inactive_is_low()` from a quarter of the LRU size. Something like:\n\n```\nSince mm/vmscan.c opted into \u003clinux/p3s_user_pages.h\u003e for the MGLRU\npage table walk, PAGE_SIZE and PAGE_SHIFT there follow the current\ntask. A 4KB task that writes \"1M\" to memory.reclaim then asks for 4MB\nof reclaim, and with MGLRU disabled, its direct reclaim sizes the\ninactive list from a quarter of the LRU. Use the kernel page size in\nuser_proactive_reclaim() and inactive_is_low().\n```\n\nNit: as on aosp/4409398, could you wrap the body at 72 columns and drop the blank line between `Bug:` and `Change-Id:`?",
